00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:10.510
about 150 packages of electrolytes.

269
00:11:10.510 --> 00:11:11.343
Elements?

270
00:11:11.343 --> 00:11:13.330
Elements, so they're either terrified

271
00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:15.480
that I'm going to fall on my face at some point,

272
00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:16.630
or just want me to try it.

273
00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:20.530
So I use that during the first simulation,

274
00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.370
I didn't hydrate very well,

275
00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:24.000
I didn't have it planned out very well.

276
00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.780
The second one, I had the element stuff

277
00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:31.030
which really helped, I hydrated and ate much more mindfully

278
00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:31.863
and it was working.

279
00:11:31.863 --> 00:11:35.210
And I have a dozen Japanese sweet potatoes

280
00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:38.490
those small ones, that I'm gonna cook ahead of time.

281
00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:40.520
I'm gonna have a lot of avocados in the house.

282
00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:43.281
Soak some dates too, those are good.

283
00:11:43.281 --> 00:11:44.530
Yeah, dates, I can get dates, I can get dates.

284
00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:47.550
That's great, man, no stomach problems?

285
00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:48.383
You know, what's funny,

286
00:11:48.383 --> 00:11:53.360
what's good about the Friday simulation,

287
00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:54.810
it just so happened I woke up

288
00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:57.610
with like a little bit of a weird digestive thing

289
00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:00.000
and one of those headaches that's kind of like

290
00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.790
those nine kind of almost food poisoning, headaches.

291
00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:04.547
And I woke up with it and I went running

292
00:12:04.547 --> 00:12:08.340
and the first two miles of the first run, I felt it.

293
00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:09.860
And then I finally ran through it,

294
00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:11.970
and then the second run, same thing

295
00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:13.090
'cause I hadn't hydrated enough.

296
00:12:13.090 --> 00:12:15.070
After the second run, I really made sure

297
00:12:15.070 --> 00:12:18.130
I did two electrolyte 16 ounces

298
00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:20.080
and then that kind of washed it out

299
00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:22.234
and I felt great by the end.

300
00:12:22.234 --> 00:12:25.900
Yeah, I mean, that's why one of many reasons

301
00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:28.320
why doing the simulations are so important

302
00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:30.718
because you're putting yourself in the position

303
00:12:30.718 --> 00:12:34.680
that simulates what you're gonna feel like in that moment

304
00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:37.980
and you're able to test things like hydration, et cetera.

305
00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:41.470
The other thing that I thought that you said that was great

306
00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:44.170
is that you began running and you didn't feel good

307
00:12:44.170 --> 00:12:45.780
and you kept going and that shifted.

308
00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.510
And I think that's a really important lesson

309
00:12:48.510 --> 00:12:50.500
for anybody who's listening, who is dipping their toe

310
00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.360
into the endurance world.

311
00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:54.710
There's gonna be days and moments and times

312
00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:56.220
whether it's in training or in a race

313
00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:57.690
where you're not gonna feel good

314
00:12:57.690 --> 00:12:58.910
or you're gonna start running

315
00:12:58.910 --> 00:13:01.980
and you're gonna feel terrible and think, well,

316
00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:04.230
I don't have it, I need to quit.

317
00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:07.550
But if you just stay in it, you realize and you learn

318
00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:10.710
that things change and shift, just 'cause you feel lousy

319
00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:12.410
in one particular instance

320
00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:14.150
doesn't mean that that's gonna persist.

321
00:13:14.150 --> 00:13:16.290
Like you can kind of work through that

322
00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:18.250
and you have these breakthroughs

323
00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:20.580
when you do these simulation weekends and you realize,

324
00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:23.570
oh yeah, I got through that, I ended up finishing that run

325
00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:25.930
feeling better than when I started,

326
00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:28.730
and that's very empowering in terms of providing you

327
00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:30.890
with the confidence and the experience

328
00:13:30.890 --> 00:13:32.870
to whether something like this.

329
00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:34.350
Thank you, that's it, that's what I felt.

330
00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:36.660
I felt like, okay, the headache's not great,

331
00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:38.803
but it's not the worst headache I've ever had,

332
00:13:38.803 --> 00:13:40.257
so I'm gonna do it and I'm gonna look at it.

333
00:13:40.257 --> 00:13:42.040
And we slept horribly the night before,

334
00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:46.023
the baby was really restless and so I felt like good,

335
00:13:47.781 --> 00:13:49.981
I felt confident, like this is a good thing,

336
00:13:51.244 --> 00:13:52.550
let's see if I can do it now,

337
00:13:52.550 --> 00:13:54.640
so that's how the simulation started,

338
00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:56.630
and it ended like a lot better.

339
00:13:56.630 --> 00:13:59.030
The rough part's gonna be those like ones

340
00:13:59.030 --> 00:14:01.700
in the middle of the night or in the early morning.

341
00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:03.272
That's gonna be tough for me, it's gonna be tough.

342
00:14:03.272 --> 00:14:04.510
I'm just gonna get he first night,

343
00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:06.560
I'm gonna stay up to the midnight run,

344
00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:09.340
I'm not gonna try to get any sleep until after midnight,

345
00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:11.600
and then do the midnight run,

346
00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:13.820
then get a little bit of sleep, get up for the four

347
00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:17.300
get a little more sleep and then try to stay awake all day.

348
00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:18.599
That's the plan.

349
00:14:18.599 --> 00:14:21.100
Well, I've got a ride plan for Saturday,

350
00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:23.070
so maybe on Saturday, I'll ride down

351
00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:26.311
to your neck of the woods and try to track you down.

352
00:14:26.311 --> 00:14:27.897
Hell yeah, that'd be amazing.

353
00:14:28.926 --> 00:14:29.759
And I'll grab your phone

354
00:14:29.759 --> 00:14:30.592
and do the Instagram thing.

355
00:14:30.592 --> 00:14:31.425
That'd be amazing.

356
00:14:31.425 --> 00:14:35.930
Yeah, speaking of riding, that's really been something

357
00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:38.023
that I've been focusing on lately.

358
00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:41.870
I've just formed this new ambassador relationship

359
00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:45.860
with specialized bicycles which is really great.

360
00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:50.860
And they've got me kitted out on this new Turbo Creo SL,

361
00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:56.500
and I put gravel tires on that and I've been getting out

362
00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:59.480
