392
00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.200
which is something I have no experience with

393
00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:16.890
and never thought in a million years

394
00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:18.010
that I would ever have an e-bike,

395
00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:20.220
like I'm a fitness junkie,

396
00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:22.830
I don't wanna motor in my bike, I'm gonna test myself.

397
00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.330
You gotta be some kind of lame,

398
00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.308
like put a motor on your bike-

399
00:16:27.308 --> 00:16:28.880
Just say limo, you'll get canceled.

400
00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:32.414
I don't know what the appropriate vernacular is anymore.

401
00:16:32.414 --> 00:16:33.259
(laughs) Just kidding.

402
00:16:33.259 --> 00:16:34.300
But I had two experiences.

403
00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:37.720
One, I went up to Santa Barbara a couple months ago

404
00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:39.590
to hang out with Dan Buettner

405
00:16:39.590 --> 00:16:41.240
and he's got a bunch of e-bikes

406
00:16:41.240 --> 00:16:43.217
and he's like, you gotta ride these are super fun.

407
00:16:43.217 --> 00:16:44.740
And I was like, a e-bike really?

408
00:16:44.740 --> 00:16:46.740
And we took them out and we had a blast,

409
00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:50.140
went all over Santa Barbara up all these climbs, super fun

410
00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:54.300
and then I had Bryan Fogel on the podcast who people know

411
00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:56.307
