So my question is I'm a family physician

2041
01:30:34.350 --> 01:30:37.380
who works full time, I have twin three year olds

2042
01:30:37.380 --> 01:30:40.883
and I am trying to dabble in ultra running.

2043
01:30:41.870 --> 01:30:44.380
My wife is supportive of my running

2044
01:30:44.380 --> 01:30:48.120
but in a way that can be frustrating

2045
01:30:48.120 --> 01:30:49.750
and difficult for our relationship.

2046
01:30:49.750 --> 01:30:54.750
So my question is how do I best balance these three things

2047
01:30:55.300 --> 01:30:59.130
that I have going on without disrupting the balance

2048
01:30:59.130 --> 01:31:03.370
of my relationships as well, specifically with longer runs

2049
01:31:03.370 --> 01:31:05.960
on the weekends and time away from family?

2050
01:31:05.960 --> 01:31:09.590
What is a good way to address these issues

2051
01:31:09.590 --> 01:31:11.280
and have everyone's needs met?

2052
01:31:11.280 --> 01:31:12.260
Thanks guys, bye.

2053
01:31:12.260 --> 01:31:15.480
This is a great question, I think this is relatable

2054
01:31:15.480 --> 01:31:20.280
for anybody who gets involved in endurance sports.

2055
01:31:20.280 --> 01:31:25.280
The term Ironman widow exists for a reason,

2056
01:31:26.350 --> 01:31:28.930
because these pursuits can often end

2057
01:31:28.930 --> 01:31:32.240
in cataclysmic relationship results,

2058
01:31:32.240 --> 01:31:33.813
if not handled appropriately so-

2059
01:31:33.813 --> 01:31:35.930
I figured you are the perfect person to ask this question.

2060
01:31:35.930 --> 01:31:37.090
Well, it's not easy.

2061
01:31:37.090 --> 01:31:38.640
I mean, this is the first thing I would say

2062
01:31:38.640 --> 01:31:42.780
is you're set up for failure right out of the gate

2063
01:31:42.780 --> 01:31:47.340
because this is a very difficult hat trick to accomplish.

2064
01:31:47.340 --> 01:31:50.460
And I think to launch into this

2065
01:31:50.460 --> 01:31:53.360
the first thing to bear in mind is you can't excel

2066
01:31:53.360 --> 01:31:55.310
at all of these things every single day.

2067
01:31:55.310 --> 01:31:57.160
Like, there's this idea of how am I gonna balance

2068
01:31:57.160 --> 01:31:59.880
all of these things so that I'm giving them

2069
01:31:59.880 --> 01:32:02.510
an appropriate amount of attention every single day.

2070
01:32:02.510 --> 01:32:04.880
And I think that's the wrong way to think about it

2071
01:32:04.880 --> 01:32:06.150
because you can't do that.

2072
01:32:06.150 --> 01:32:10.710
You can't be at your best as a physician, as a partner

2073
01:32:10.710 --> 01:32:14.040
as a parent, and as an athlete all the time,

2074
01:32:14.040 --> 01:32:16.320
like it's just not rigged that way.

2075
01:32:16.320 --> 01:32:19.890
So let go of that fantasy out of the gate

2076
01:32:19.890 --> 01:32:23.930
and try to configure a schedule and a structure

2077
01:32:23.930 --> 01:32:28.930
that allows you to kind of toggle between these pursuits,

2078
01:32:29.000 --> 01:32:31.690
understanding that on certain days

2079
01:32:31.690 --> 01:32:35.060
your priority is gonna be in one of these buckets

2080
01:32:35.060 --> 01:32:38.080
or two of these buckets, but not all of these buckets.

2081
01:32:38.080 --> 01:32:41.300
So that over the course of a month or a week

2082
01:32:41.300 --> 01:32:43.640
they're all getting an adequate amount of attention

2083
01:32:43.640 --> 01:32:47.260
but not all on the same day or at the same time.

2084
01:32:47.260 --> 01:32:50.630
So structure and scheduling super important.

2085
01:32:50.630 --> 01:32:55.630
I think that you should craft that schedule in cooperation

2086
01:32:55.730 --> 01:32:57.980
and partnership with your wife

2087
01:32:57.980 --> 01:33:00.730
so that your wife is part of organizing

2088
01:33:00.730 --> 01:33:03.150
what these days are gonna look like

2089
01:33:03.150 --> 01:33:07.640
that your wife is participating, in the allocation

2090
01:33:07.640 --> 01:33:12.640
of your time and energy and to come to that conversation,

2091
01:33:14.200 --> 01:33:17.320
trying or endeavoring to the best of your ability

2092
01:33:17.320 --> 01:33:20.880
to structure your training at periods of time

2093
01:33:20.880 --> 01:33:25.210
that don't compromise the goals that your wife has

2094
01:33:25.210 --> 01:33:29.100
or the parenting needs that you both mutually share.

2095
01:33:29.100 --> 01:33:31.040
So that might mean that your runs

2096
01:33:31.040 --> 01:33:33.840
have to be super early in the morning before anybody's awake

2097
01:33:33.840 --> 01:33:35.640
or late at night when everybody's asleep.

2098
01:33:35.640 --> 01:33:38.120
And I understand that you have a full-time job,

2099
01:33:38.120 --> 01:33:40.240
you're not a professional ultra runner, though,

2100
01:33:40.240 --> 01:33:41.400
nobody's paying you to do that,

2101
01:33:41.400 --> 01:33:43.250
this is something you choose to do

2102
01:33:43.250 --> 01:33:46.800
but you've got to make the choice of how you apply that

2103
01:33:46.800 --> 01:33:48.710
in a way that's not disruptive to your family,

2104
01:33:48.710 --> 01:33:49.900
you already know that.

2105
01:33:49.900 --> 01:33:54.690
And that means finding those windows of opportunity

2106
01:33:54.690 --> 01:33:58.730
that don't put your wife's schedule at peril

2107
01:33:58.730 --> 01:34:01.223
and create this tension in the relationship.

2108
01:34:02.920 --> 01:34:06.500
The other thing is you don't wanna ever set yourself

2109
01:34:06.500 --> 01:34:09.190
up to be overtrained or overly fatigued,

2110
01:34:09.190 --> 01:34:10.920
you've got to be able to show up a hundred percent

2111
01:34:10.920 --> 01:34:13.569
for your kids and for your wife when you're not training

2112
01:34:13.569 --> 01:34:14.719
and you're not working.

2113
01:34:17.876 --> 01:34:20.010
So that doesn't become an additional drag

2114
01:34:20.010 --> 01:34:23.450
on top of the hour spent when you're not at home.

2115
01:34:23.450 --> 01:34:26.440
And I think what's been helpful to me

2116
01:34:26.440 --> 01:34:27.760
in doing this is twofold.

2117
01:34:27.760 --> 01:34:29.930
First anticipate your wife's needs

2118
01:34:29.930 --> 01:34:32.450
and your kids' needs in advance,

2119
01:34:32.450 --> 01:34:34.103
so that you're planning for that,

2120
01:34:35.230 --> 01:34:38.030
and you're not like showing up,

2121
01:34:38.030 --> 01:34:39.370
oh you didn't get the groceries

2122
01:34:39.370 --> 01:34:41.290
'cause you had to go running or something like that.

2123
01:34:41.290 --> 01:34:43.220
These are the things that like are small things

2124
01:34:43.220 --> 01:34:44.840
in isolation, but they add up

2125
01:34:44.840 --> 01:34:48.300
and they can really derail a relationship.

2126
01:34:48.300 --> 01:34:52.220
So being ahead of the curve in terms of understanding

2127
01:34:52.220 --> 01:34:55.410
and anticipating what your wife is gonna need

2128
01:34:55.410 --> 01:34:58.630
and fulfilling those needs before perhaps she's even aware

2129
01:34:58.630 --> 01:34:59.830
that she needs them filled.

2130
01:34:59.830 --> 01:35:02.810
So that way you're demonstrating through your behavior

2131
01:35:02.810 --> 01:35:05.900
repetitive behavior, that you're conscious

2132
01:35:05.900 --> 01:35:08.470
of the fact that you're also running

2133
01:35:08.470 --> 01:35:10.730
is perhaps taking you away from the relationship

2134
01:35:10.730 --> 01:35:12.890
more than she would like but you're showing up

2135
01:35:12.890 --> 01:35:17.890
in ways that are telling her like you're here, right.

2136
01:35:17.940 --> 01:35:20.220
Even when you're not there, you're actually there,

2137
01:35:20.220 --> 01:35:23.170
and then when you are there to be a hundred percent.

2138
01:35:23.170 --> 01:35:25.660
Like when I was trained for Ultraman at my peak,

2139
01:35:25.660 --> 01:35:28.210
I've told this story before, but I come back

2140
01:35:28.210 --> 01:35:31.690
from like a 30 mile run or a six hour bike ride

2141
01:35:31.690 --> 01:35:34.260
and I'd walk in the house like just wasted.

2142
01:35:34.260 --> 01:35:35.890
And Julie would like hand me a baby

2143
01:35:35.890 --> 01:35:38.747
and be like your turn bye, I'm gonna go do my thing.

2144
01:35:38.747 --> 01:35:41.930
And I couldn't be like, I need a nap or I gotta like shower,

2145
01:35:41.930 --> 01:35:45.800
it's like, no, you gotta be on point, it's your turn.

2146
01:35:45.800 --> 01:35:49.290
And by respecting that and making sure

2147
01:35:49.290 --> 01:35:54.140
that I was present when those moments arose,

2148
01:35:54.140 --> 01:35:56.350
that's how we were able to kind of keep everything

2149
01:35:56.350 --> 01:35:57.350
moving and on track.

2150
01:35:57.350 --> 01:35:59.053
If I was just like, no I can't

2151
01:35:59.053 --> 01:36:02.020
or sorry I gotta train right now,

2152
01:36:02.020 --> 01:36:04.000
like that's not gonna work.

2153
01:36:04.000 --> 01:36:06.390
Were there times where she pushed back

2154
01:36:06.390 --> 01:36:08.838
against, like super long?

2155
01:36:08.838 --> 01:36:11.336
I mean, I was lucky because I have her very supportive.

2156
01:36:11.336 --> 01:36:12.980
She's all about you finding like-

2157
01:36:12.980 --> 01:36:15.010
Right, and that doesn't mean that it wasn't hard

2158
01:36:15.010 --> 01:36:17.000
because we're talking about a ton of time.

2159
01:36:17.000 --> 01:36:20.257
And also, we were going through some financial stuff,

2160
01:36:20.257 --> 01:36:21.190
it was like a very difficult period.

2161
01:36:21.190 --> 01:36:24.490
And I credit Julie tremendously

2162
01:36:24.490 --> 01:36:28.370
for really being an incredible support

2163
01:36:28.370 --> 01:36:31.350
in a way that I think most partners wouldn't

2164
01:36:31.350 --> 01:36:33.240
and can't be expected to, honestly.

2165
01:36:33.240 --> 01:36:34.840
So it's understandable,

2166
01:36:34.840 --> 01:36:37.409
like what you're gonna go run for...

2167
01:36:37.409 --> 01:36:39.930
Like we have twin baby, like, what are you doing?

2168
01:36:39.930 --> 01:36:41.580
Like you gotta be here.

2169
01:36:41.580 --> 01:36:45.430
So that's why I think anticipating your partner's needs

2170
01:36:45.430 --> 01:36:48.570
and the needs of your children is so important.

2171
01:36:48.570 --> 01:36:51.450
I also think that you have to choose your moments.

2172
01:36:51.450 --> 01:36:54.448
Like I said, at the outset, it's impossible to excel

2173
01:36:54.448 --> 01:36:55.281
at all of these things every single day,

2174
01:36:55.281 --> 01:36:56.670
and if you attempt this you're gonna fail

2175
01:36:56.670 --> 01:36:58.340
in all the categories.

2176
01:36:58.340 --> 01:37:00.050
You're not gonna be able to train like a pro,

2177
01:37:00.050 --> 01:37:02.560
So don't try to, and there's gonna be days

2178
01:37:02.560 --> 01:37:05.980
where maybe you have some big run on your calendar

2179
01:37:05.980 --> 01:37:07.220
and this is really important to you

2180
01:37:07.220 --> 01:37:10.360
but something went haywire at home and the kids need you

2181
01:37:10.360 --> 01:37:12.820
and you gotta be like, what are my priorities?

2182
01:37:12.820 --> 01:37:13.770
Like I gotta show up for my kids,

2183
01:37:13.770 --> 01:37:15.650
I gotta show up for my wife.

2184
01:37:15.650 --> 01:37:18.790
Like what is most important in the grand scheme of things?

2185
01:37:18.790 --> 01:37:21.220
Is it really worth derailing your relationship

2186
01:37:21.220 --> 01:37:22.053
for ultra running?

2187
01:37:22.053 --> 01:37:24.520
Like ultra running is something you can do your whole life

2188
01:37:24.520 --> 01:37:28.701
if you do it responsibly and so that doesn't mean

2189
01:37:28.701 --> 01:37:31.970
that your needs shouldn't be met either.

2190
01:37:31.970 --> 01:37:34.390
It's important If this is bringing you happiness

2191
01:37:34.390 --> 01:37:37.490
and fulfillment that you should have the freedom

2192
01:37:37.490 --> 01:37:41.700
and the license to like do the things that you enjoy doing

2193
01:37:41.700 --> 01:37:44.823
which is why communication is so important.

2194
01:37:45.680 --> 01:37:47.200
And if this is important to you,

2195
01:37:47.200 --> 01:37:52.200
it's incumbent upon you to communicate the importance of it

2196
01:37:52.360 --> 01:37:54.750
to your wife, so that she really understands.

2197
01:37:54.750 --> 01:37:57.400
Like she really understand why is this important to you?

2198
01:37:57.400 --> 01:37:59.390
Why are you doing this?

2199
01:37:59.390 --> 01:38:01.330
And the more that you can have

2200
01:38:01.330 --> 01:38:05.180
that channel of communication open with your wife,

2201
01:38:05.180 --> 01:38:09.370
I think you'll be in a better place to engender the empathy

2202
01:38:09.370 --> 01:38:11.330
and support that you're looking for.

2203
01:38:11.330 --> 01:38:12.360
But that's a two-way street,

2204
01:38:12.360 --> 01:38:14.037
you gotta give it in return as well.

2205
01:38:14.037 --> 01:38:16.910
You can't expect her to support you

2206
01:38:16.910 --> 01:38:18.490
unless you're supporting her in kind.

2207
01:38:18.490 --> 01:38:21.920
So what is your wife's ultra running?

2208
01:38:21.920 --> 01:38:24.430
Like, what is it that she would like to be doing?

2209
01:38:24.430 --> 01:38:26.930
And how can you go out of your way to make sure

2210
01:38:26.930 --> 01:38:30.060
that you're supportive to her in that regard

2211
01:38:30.060 --> 01:38:33.160
in the way that you would like to be supported?

2212
01:38:33.160 --> 01:38:36.410
It's great advice, I can't offer anything

2213
01:38:36.410 --> 01:38:38.290
to relate to this discussion other than,

2214
01:38:38.290 --> 01:38:39.123
'cause I'm not doing 30 miles-

2215
01:38:39.123 --> 01:38:40.940
But you have a baby and you're trying to do

2216
01:38:40.940 --> 01:38:42.900
this Goggins thing and you've got a show at home,

2217
01:38:42.900 --> 01:38:44.217
so how's that going?

2218
01:38:44.217 --> 01:38:46.670
I had to talk her into the Goggins thing.

2219
01:38:46.670 --> 01:38:48.688
She was not really feeling the Goggins thing.

2220
01:38:48.688 --> 01:38:51.340
(laughing)

2221
01:38:51.340 --> 01:38:54.910
Well, 'cause for her, she's like with the baby

2222
01:38:54.910 --> 01:38:58.730
almost all the time and I have my work,

2223
01:38:58.730 --> 01:39:02.300
which at least allows me even if I'm in the same apartment,

2224
01:39:02.300 --> 01:39:04.720
I'm in a psychic space, that is my own.

2225
01:39:04.720 --> 01:39:07.700
And she's not really permitted to psychic space

2226
01:39:07.700 --> 01:39:09.870
that is her own too often.

2227
01:39:09.870 --> 01:39:13.200
And so when I run training off and I'll take the baby out

2228
01:39:13.200 --> 01:39:15.500
with me in a stroller run

2229
01:39:15.500 --> 01:39:16.610
Right, that was the other thing I had

2230
01:39:16.610 --> 01:39:19.393
on my list of things to respond to,

2231
01:39:19.393 --> 01:39:24.393
like get the twin baby carriage thing,

2232
01:39:24.640 --> 01:39:25.544
is that what's it's called?

2233
01:39:25.544 --> 01:39:26.377
I haven't had babies in a while, what do you call them?

2234
01:39:26.377 --> 01:39:27.690
Strollers.
Yeah, strollers, (laughs).

2235
01:39:28.792 --> 01:39:31.490
It's been awhile, but it's still called strollers.

2236
01:39:31.490 --> 01:39:32.440
And she lives in Long Beach.

2237
01:39:32.440 --> 01:39:35.400
There's like those paths along the ocean,

2238
01:39:35.400 --> 01:39:37.400
where you can like push a stroller and-

2239
01:39:37.400 --> 01:39:40.600
Pretty soon they can ride bikes alongside you or whatever.

2240
01:39:40.600 --> 01:39:44.090
So I did have to talk her into that and it just took that.

2241
01:39:44.090 --> 01:39:46.150
I would explain to her why it was important to me

2242
01:39:46.150 --> 01:39:48.230
the best I could, even though I couldn't really explain

2243
01:39:48.230 --> 01:39:51.110
to you why it's important to me, but she understood that,

2244
01:39:51.110 --> 01:39:52.050
she never didn't want me to do it.

2245
01:39:52.050 --> 01:39:54.640
And it doesn't really show up as much in the running

2246
01:39:54.640 --> 01:39:58.440
'cause for me, most of my runs are a little over an hour

2247
01:39:58.440 --> 01:40:01.285
sometimes less, sometimes a little over an hour.

2248
01:40:01.285 --> 01:40:02.360
And if I wanna do a long one for me,

2249
01:40:02.360 --> 01:40:03.820
it's like a 10 mile run usually,

2250
01:40:03.820 --> 01:40:07.000
so that's like, it's not like a 30 mile run.

2251
01:40:07.000 --> 01:40:11.130
But swimming, at least doing the dives in Malibu

2252
01:40:11.130 --> 01:40:13.955
that has become a lot less frequent

2253
01:40:13.955 --> 01:40:14.788
than it used to be for me.

2254
01:40:14.788 --> 01:40:15.860
I try to get us out there once a week

2255
01:40:15.860 --> 01:40:18.570
but that includes taking everybody out

2256
01:40:18.570 --> 01:40:21.330
getting a beach tent set up, doing the whole thing,

2257
01:40:21.330 --> 01:40:22.163
otherwise-

2258
01:40:22.163 --> 01:40:24.790
As somebody who participated in that with you,

2259
01:40:24.790 --> 01:40:28.040
I can affirm that that is a languishing affair.

2260
01:40:28.040 --> 01:40:30.970
That goes on for hours unnecessarily.

2261
01:40:30.970 --> 01:40:32.840
I'm like, are we gonna swim and get this done?

2262
01:40:32.840 --> 01:40:33.673
What are we doing?

2263
01:40:33.673 --> 01:40:36.150
We're looking for our octopus T-shirt.

2264
01:40:36.150 --> 01:40:38.040
I'm like I'm out for a workout,

2265
01:40:38.040 --> 01:40:39.550
and you're looking for octopus.

2266
01:40:39.550 --> 01:40:42.470
Yes, that's right, we're getting in touch,

2267
01:40:42.470 --> 01:40:43.610
with our lyric escape.

2268
01:40:43.610 --> 01:40:45.570
Yeah, I'm like, no wonder.

2269
01:40:45.570 --> 01:40:47.237
She's like, what are you doing?

2270
01:40:47.237 --> 01:40:48.180
Get back here.

2271
01:40:48.180 --> 01:40:49.550
She comes out with us, so she's only been able to...

2272
01:40:49.550 --> 01:40:52.590
She went one time, she doesn't like 55 degree water,

2273
01:40:52.590 --> 01:40:54.680
so for her it's like if the visit is good

2274
01:40:54.680 --> 01:40:56.840
and it's warmish she's down.

2275
01:40:56.840 --> 01:40:59.040
And so we have made it possible for her

2276
01:40:59.040 --> 01:41:01.610
to go with the group and then I did my own thing after,

2277
01:41:01.610 --> 01:41:04.010
we've done that once but it does take,

2278
01:41:04.010 --> 01:41:06.530
like, I can't expect her to go sit on the beach

2279
01:41:06.530 --> 01:41:07.580
when the wind is howling

2280
01:41:07.580 --> 01:41:09.470
and it's getting sandblasted with the baby

2281
01:41:09.470 --> 01:41:10.810
while I go on a little swim.

2282
01:41:10.810 --> 01:41:14.630
So that is not happening as often as it used to

2283
01:41:14.630 --> 01:41:16.150
but she loves the beach also,

2284
01:41:16.150 --> 01:41:17.360
so she likes being out there.

2285
01:41:17.360 --> 01:41:20.310
So it's really about the communication aspect is important.

2286
01:41:20.310 --> 01:41:22.620
And you do have to kinda supplement,

2287
01:41:22.620 --> 01:41:25.410
especially knowing that I have four by four coming up,

2288
01:41:25.410 --> 01:41:27.160
basically after four by four,

2289
01:41:27.160 --> 01:41:31.040
she prefers kind of workouts with this trainer, from our gym

